-- title:
--   Lemma 2.4 — $\mathrm{Vol}(A_t)$ and $\mathrm{Vol}(\overline{A_t})$ are martingales
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a temporal graph with fixed degrees and run the standard two-opinion voter model on $\mathcal G$ from any initial state. Let $A_t$ be the set of vertices holding opinion $0$ at time $t$ and $\overline{A_t}$ its complement. Then both
--   $$\bigl(\mathrm{Vol}(A_t):t\ge0\bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\bigl(\mathrm{Vol}(\overline{A_t}):t\ge0\bigr)$$
--   are martingales with respect to the history filtration $(\sigma(\mathcal H_t):t\ge0)$.
--
--   Fixed degrees make a vertex of opinion $1$ switch to $0$ exactly as likely, in volume, as the reverse; this is the basic conservation law behind the analysis of the voter model.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the voter process (ξ_t : t ≥ 0) of Definition 1.2 on some probability space → the path measure voterLaw on ℕ → (V → Fin k), built by Ionescu-Tulcea (Kernel.traj) from the synchronous lazy step kernels of Definition 1.2, started at σ₀; reason: the process is constructed from its definition (paper.md R4); every event and expectation of the paper is one of this law
--   - encoding: filtration σ(H_t) generated by the history H_t = (A_0, …, A_t) → Filtration.piLE t on the path space (σ-algebra of ξ_0, …, ξ_t); reason: for two opinions ξ_s and A_s determine each other, so the σ-algebras coincide
--   - encoding: a sequence of undirected graphs on a common vertex set V(G) with common degree d(v) → T : TemporalGraph V: a Fintype V, G t : SimpleGraph V, and the degree data d with degree_eq and one_le_d; reason: the paper's graphs are plain finite graphs (n vertices, m = ½ ∑ d(v) edges, e_t counts edges); no loop or parallel edge occurs in them, the self-loop of Figure 1 only pictures laziness
-- source:
--   Rocha Avila, Dell, Lapinskas, Temporal Conductance and Bounds on the Voter Model for Dynamic Networks, arXiv:2606.13374 (2 Nov 2026), Lemma 2.4, p.12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TemporalVoter_minoritySet

open scoped Classical
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace TemporalVoter

/-- **Lemma 2.4** (arXiv:2606.13374, version of 2 Nov 2026, p.12): in the standard two-opinion
voter model on a temporal graph with fixed degrees, from any initial state `σ₀`, the volumes
`(Vol(A_t) : t ≥ 0)` of the opinion-0 set and `(Vol(Ā_t) : t ≥ 0)` of its complement are
martingales under the history filtration `(σ(H_t) : t ≥ 0)`.

**Formalization Note** `σ(H_t)` is `Filtration.piLE t` on the path space, the σ-algebra generated
by `ξ_0, …, ξ_t` (Definition 2.3, p.12). -/
theorem lemma_2_4 {V : Type} [Fintype V] (T : TemporalGraph V) (σ₀ : V → Fin 2) :
    Martingale (fun t ω => T.vol (opinionZeroSet (ω t)))
        (Filtration.piLE (X := fun _ : ℕ => V → Fin 2)) (voterLaw T 2 σ₀) ∧
      Martingale (fun t ω => T.vol (opinionZeroSet (ω t))ᶜ)
        (Filtration.piLE (X := fun _ : ℕ => V → Fin 2)) (voterLaw T 2 σ₀) := by sorry

end TemporalVoter
